 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Leave it at the sink, not in the pits. Some campsites won't want it in the pits anyway. Even with eco soap, it' still better for the ground. Try not to bury them. Put them in a small bin with the other rubbish, or spread them thinly so birds can take them. It' small price to pay. Most campsites appreciate it, too. Good. And bring a small bottle of hot water to top up everyone's water bottle every couple of days.",
